(2710900, 372713, 20056, '<td valign="top">Thanks everybody for your comments, I also liked the image... maybe people got tired of chess pictures too; that''s why so low score :) Never mind!<br/> <br/>In my opinion different cameras give different tones: I love how nikon produce the yellows but olympus give You also INCREDIBLES colors and very REAL: so if You have a good woodboard then You get good results :)<br/> <br/>Basically my pp is pretty common: cropping, levels, curves, contrast (using unshrap mask) , a little warming, a touch of color balance in LAB mode...and size and sharpening, thats all. <br/> <br/>I forgot: lenses also help :)</td>', 'Thanks everybody for your comments, I also liked the image... maybe people got tired of chess pictures too; that''s why so low score :) Never mind! In my opinion different cameras give different tones: I love how nikon produce the yellows but olympus give You also INCREDIBLES colors and very REAL: so if You have a good woodboard then You get good results :) Basically my pp is pretty common: cropping, levels, curves, contrast (using unshrap mask) , a little warming, a touch of color balance in LAB mode...and size and sharpening, thats all.  I forgot: lenses also help :)', '2006-08-09 13:29:25.000000', NULL, 0),
